207:**Fig.S1** Distribution of normative z-scores for cortical thickness in both groups. The blue color represented the SeLECTS group, whereas the yellow color represented the control group. The dotted vertical lines represented the cutoffs for infra-normal (z-scores &lt; -1.96) and supra-normal (z-scores &gt; 1.96) values.
213:**Fig.S2** Distribution of normative z-scores for surface area in both groups. The blue color represented the SeLECTS group, whereas the yellow color represented the control group. The dotted vertical lines represented the cutoffs for infra-normal (z-scores &lt; -1.96) and supra-normal (z-scores &gt; 1.96) values.
231:**Fig.S5 Comparison of normative z-score and single observed measure.** Accuracy of diagnostic classification, employing every single regional normative deviation and observed brain morphometric measure, including (A) subcortical volume, (B) cortical thickness, and (C) cortical area. Linear support vector classification was applied to assess the diagnostic status. AUC, area under the curve; and ROC, receiver operating characteristic curve.

